## Overview

This document outlines the **code conventions, architecture patterns, and development workflow** for the EM NexaCore frontend application. It does NOT define the visual design.

> **IMPORTANT — Visual Design Source of Truth:**
>
> All visual design decisions — colors, typography, spacing, border radius, shadows, component styling, button variants, input styles, and page layouts — are defined in **`ui-design-system.md`** (design tokens and component specs extracted from Figma) and the **Figma extract JSON files** (page-level layouts with exact structure, dimensions, and content).
>
> This document (`frontend-standards.mdc`) provides **code examples for illustration purposes only**. When code examples in this document show colors, dimensions, or styling values, they are generic examples — **always defer to `ui-design-system.md` and the Figma extracts for actual values**.
>
> Hierarchy:
> 1. **Figma extract JSON** → Page structure, layout, dimensions, text content, component placement
> 2. **`ui-design-system.md`** → Design tokens (colors, typography, shadows, radii, spacing), component visual specs
> 3. **This document** → Code conventions, architecture patterns, state management, folder structure, development workflow

## Technology Stack

### Core Technologies
- **Next.js 16** (App Router, Turbopack default): React framework with server-side rendering and file-system routing. `headers()` / `cookies()` / `draftMode()` are async (must be `await`-ed). `next lint` was removed — use `eslint` directly.
- **React 19**: Modern React with functional components and hooks. `forwardRef` deprecated (still functional); ref-as-prop is the new pattern.
- **TypeScript 5**: For type safety and better development experience (TS 6 migration tracked as SCRUM-371)

### UI Framework
- **TailwindCSS 4** (CSS-based config via `@theme` in `globals.css`; no more `tailwind.config.ts`): Utility-first CSS framework. PostCSS plugin is `@tailwindcss/postcss`. Runtime-readable design tokens live at `src/lib/design-tokens.ts`.
- **CSS Variables**: Custom theming system for light/dark mode
- **Custom UI Components**: `Button`, `Input`, `Spinner`, `Divider`, `ThemeToggle`

### State Management & Data Flow
- **React Context + useReducer**: For global auth state management
- **React Context + useState**: For theme state management
- **Custom Hooks**: `useAuth()`, `useTheme()` for consuming context
- **ApiClient**: Singleton fetch-based HTTP client with token refresh

### Testing Framework
- **Jest 30** + **next/jest**: Unit testing with SWC transform (via `jest.config.mjs`). For tests that exercise navigation, **import `navigateTo()` from `@/lib/navigation` and mock that module** — jsdom 26+ (bundled with Jest 30) makes `window.location` non-writable + non-configurable, so direct `Object.defineProperty(window, 'location', ...)` mocking no longer works.
- **React Testing Library**: Component testing utilities (`@testing-library/react`, `@testing-library/user-event`)
- **jest-dom**: Custom matchers (`toBeInTheDocument()`, `toBeDisabled()`, etc.)
- **Test directory**: `tests/` at project root (mirroring `src/` structure)
- **Test file pattern**: `*.test.tsx`
- **Custom render**: `tests/test-utils.tsx` re-exports RTL with optional provider wrapper

### Visual Regression Testing (VRT)

> Added by SCRUM-379. Catches pixel-level UI changes that build/lint/unit tests cannot detect (e.g. utility-class renames, theme token resolution shifts after a major framework bump).

- **Tool**: Playwright `toHaveScreenshot()` with 0.2% pixel-diff threshold
- **Specs**: `tests/e2e/visual.spec.ts` in both `nexacore-dashboard` and `satellites/sat-cristian-garcia`
- **CI**: `.github/workflows/visual-regression.yml` — runs on every PR touching `src/`, `public/`, the visual spec, or playwright config
- **Baseline**: committed under `tests/e2e/visual.spec.ts-snapshots/` (Linux-CI-captured, platform-suffixed `*-linux.png`)
- **Update baseline** (intentional design change only — DO NOT commit local Windows/macOS snapshots):
  ```
  gh workflow run visual-regression.yml \
    -f capture_baseline=true \
    -f baseline_ref=<commit-SHA-of-good-visual> \
    -f package=both
  ```
- **Read PR diffs**: when CI fails, download the `playwright-diff-report-<PR>` artifact, open `index.html`, see side-by-side actual / expected / diff per test
- **Why CI-only**: pixel rendering varies by OS / font hinting / GPU. Snapshots captured on Windows / macOS will not match Linux CI. Same model used by Vercel, Stripe, Linear, Atlassian for VRT.
- **Override** (rare — for true "intentional change accepted"): refresh baseline via the workflow_dispatch above, then re-PR

### Development Tools
- **ESLint 9** (flat config, `eslint.config.mjs`): Code linting with Next.js rules (`eslint-config-next/core-web-vitals` + `eslint-config-next/typescript`). Run with `npx eslint "src/**/*.{ts,tsx}"` — `next lint` was removed in Next 16.
- **TypeScript**: Static type checking with strict mode
- **PostCSS**: CSS processing for TailwindCSS

