## Figma-to-Code Mapping Guide

This section defines the **exact process** for translating Figma Design Plugin extract JSON files into React/Next.js components. Every implementation MUST follow this mapping — no field invention, no layout improvisation.

### Source of Truth Hierarchy (Mandatory)

| Priority | Source | What it defines |
|----------|--------|-----------------|
| 1st | **Figma extract JSON** (`specs/*-extracted.json`) | Page structure, layout, component tree, text content, spacing |
| 2nd | **`ui-design-system.md`** | Design tokens (colors, typography, shadows, radii, spacing) |
| 3rd | **This document** (`frontend-standards.mdc`) | Code conventions, file structure, patterns — NOT visual design |

**Rule**: If a Figma extract shows 2 form fields, code MUST have exactly 2 form fields. Never add fields, sections, or layouts not present in the extract.

### JSON Structure → Component Tree

Each Figma extract JSON represents a full page. The root object is the page frame. Map the hierarchy directly to JSX:

```
Root frame (page)                    → Page component (e.g., LoginPage)
  ├── "Card" frame                   → Card wrapper <div>
  │   ├── "Container" frame          → Inner container <div>
  │   │   ├── "Header" frame         → Header section with Logo
  │   │   │   └── "Logo" rectangle   → <Image src="/em-icon.png" /> (see Images section)
  │   │   └── "Body" frame           → Body section <div>
  │   │       ├── "Title Group"      → Left column <div>
  │   │       │   ├── "Title" text   → <h1> or <h2>
  │   │       │   └── "Subtitle"     → <p>
  │   │       └── "Form" frame       → Right column <form>
  │   │           ├── "Field" frame  → Field wrapper <div>
  │   │           │   ├── "Label"    → <label>
  │   │           │   └── "Input"    → <Input /> component
  │   │           ├── "Buttons"      → Button row <div>
  │   │           └── "Actions"      → OAuth section <div>
  │   └── "Footer" frame            → Footer <div>
  │       ├── "LanguageSelector"     → LanguageSelector component
  │       └── "Actions" (links)      → Help | Privacy | Terms links
  └── "Go Back Section" frame       → Bottom navigation bar <div>
```

### Node Type Mapping

| Figma `type` | JSX Element | Notes |
|-------------|-------------|-------|
| `frame` | `<div>` | Unless it has a semantic role (form, nav, etc.) |
| `text` | `<p>`, `<h1>`-`<h6>`, `<span>`, `<label>` | Choose by semantic role — see Text Mapping below |
| `rectangle` (named "Logo") | `<Image />` | Rectangle with IMAGE fill = image asset |
| `rectangle` (named "Line Left/Right") | `<div>` with `border-top` or `<hr>` | Divider lines |
| `component` | Custom React component | Map by component name (e.g., `LanguageSelector/Trigger`) |

### Text Mapping Rules

Map text nodes by their **name** and **context**, not just their type:

| Text `name` | JSX Element | Tailwind Classes |
|-------------|-------------|-----------------|
| `"Title"` | `<h1>` or `<h2>` | `text-2xl font-semibold` (from fontSize 24, fontWeight 600) |
| `"Subtitle"` | `<p>` | `text-sm` (fontSize 14) + opacity from fills |
| `"Label"` | `<label>` | `text-[15px]` (fontSize 15, fontWeight 400) |
| `"Placeholder"` | `placeholder` attr on `<input>` | NOT a separate element — use the `characters` value as placeholder text |
| `"Text"` (inside button) | Button text content | `text-base font-semibold` (fontSize 16, fontWeight 600) |
| `"Link *"` | `<a>` or `<Link>` | `text-sm font-medium` (fontSize 14, fontWeight 500) |
| `"Or"` | `<span>` inside divider | `text-xs` (fontSize 12) + opacity |
| `"Select language"` | Text inside LanguageSelector | `text-sm font-medium` |

### Layout Property Mapping

Figma Auto Layout properties map directly to Tailwind flexbox:

| Figma Property | Tailwind / CSS |
|---------------|---------------|
| `layoutMode: "HORIZONTAL"` | `flex flex-row` |
| `layoutMode: "VERTICAL"` | `flex flex-col` |
| `itemSpacing: N` | `gap-[Npx]` (or closest Tailwind spacing token) |
| `padding: { top, right, bottom, left }` | `p-[Npx]` or `pt-[T] pr-[R] pb-[B] pl-[L]` |
| `primaryAxisAlignItems: "CENTER"` | `justify-center` |
| `primaryAxisAlignItems: "MAX"` | `justify-end` |
| `counterAxisAlignItems: "CENTER"` | `items-center` |
| `layoutAlign: "STRETCH"` | `self-stretch` or `w-full` |
| `layoutGrow: 1` | `flex-1` |
| `primaryAxisSizingMode: "FIXED"` + width | `w-[Npx]` |
| `counterAxisSizingMode: "AUTO"` | Height/width auto (no explicit class needed) |

### Style Property Mapping

| Figma Property | Tailwind / CSS |
|---------------|---------------|
| `fills: [{ hex: "#fbfbfb" }]` | `bg-[#fbfbfb]` or semantic token from ui-design-system.md |
| `fills: [{ hex, opacity: 0.5 }]` | `text-content-primary/50` or `bg-[hex]/[opacity*100]` |
| `fills: [{ hex, type: "IMAGE" }]` | Replace with `<Image />` — see Images section |
| `cornerRadius: 24` | `rounded-3xl` (or `rounded-[24px]`) |
| `cornerRadius: 8` | `rounded-lg` |
| `cornerRadius: 6` | `rounded-md` |
| `strokes: [{ hex, opacity, weight }]` | `border border-[hex]/[opacity*100]` |
| `effects: [{ type: "DROP_SHADOW" }]` | `shadow-card` (from ui-design-system.md token) |

### Icon Mapping (Lucide)

Icons in Figma extracts appear as frames named `lucide/{icon-name}` with rectangle children (the vectors). **Ignore the rectangle children** — use the frame name to import from `lucide-react`:

```typescript
// Figma extract: { type: "frame", name: "lucide/mail", ... }
import { Mail } from 'lucide-react';
<Mail size={20} className="text-content-primary/50" />

// Figma extract: { type: "frame", name: "lucide/eye", ... }
import { Eye } from 'lucide-react';
<Eye size={20} className="text-content-primary/50" />

// Figma extract: { type: "frame", name: "lucide/github", ... }
import { Github } from 'lucide-react';
<Github size={20} className="text-content-primary/50" />

// Figma extract: { type: "frame", name: "lucide/chromium", ... }
// Note: "chromium" is used for Google icon in Figma. Use Chrome from lucide-react:
import { Chrome } from 'lucide-react';
<Chrome size={20} className="text-content-primary/50" />

// Figma extract: { type: "frame", name: "lucide/chevron-down", ... }
import { ChevronDown } from 'lucide-react';
<ChevronDown size={24} className="text-black/75" />

// Figma extract: { type: "frame", name: "lucide/house", ... }
import { House } from 'lucide-react';
<House size={20} className="text-black/75" />
```

**Mapping rule**: Take `lucide/{name}`, convert `{name}` from kebab-case to PascalCase, import from `lucide-react`. Icon `size` comes from the frame's `width`/`height`. Icon color comes from the children's stroke `hex` + `opacity`.

### Image Handling

The Figma plugin cannot export actual image data. When an extract contains:
- A `rectangle` named **"Logo"** → Use `<Image src="/em-icon.png" />` (the EM icon at `public/em-icon.png`)
- A fill with `type: "IMAGE"` → Identify the asset from context/name and use the local file

**Available local assets:**
- `em-icon.png` — EM icon logo (black on transparent, 72×36 in Figma)
- `em-wordmark.png` — Full EMILLION wordmark

### Complete Mapping Example

Given this Figma extract fragment:
```json
{
  "type": "frame", "name": "Email Field",
  "layoutMode": "VERTICAL", "itemSpacing": 8,
  "children": [
    { "type": "text", "name": "Label", "characters": "Email", "fontSize": 15 },
    {
      "type": "frame", "name": "Input", "cornerRadius": 8,
      "fills": [{ "hex": "#ffffff" }],
      "strokes": [{ "hex": "#000000", "opacity": 0.05, "weight": 1 }],
      "layoutMode": "HORIZONTAL", "padding": { "top": 12, "right": 16, "bottom": 12, "left": 16 },
      "children": [
        { "type": "frame", "name": "lucide/mail", "width": 20, "height": 20 },
        { "type": "text", "name": "Placeholder", "characters": "your@email.com", "fontSize": 15 }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

Produces this JSX:
```tsx
<div className="flex flex-col gap-2">
  <label className="text-[15px] text-content-primary">Email</label>
  <div className="flex items-center gap-2 rounded-lg border border-black/5 bg-white px-4 py-3">
    <Mail size={20} className="text-content-primary/50" />
    <input
      type="email"
      placeholder="your@email.com"
      className="flex-1 bg-transparent text-[15px] outline-none placeholder:text-content-primary/30"
    />
  </div>
</div>
